      "body": "Updates `nltk` to address GHSA-j456-xh4h-cpf2.\n\nEvidence:\n- `pyproject.toml` pinned `nltk==3.10.3`\n- osv-scanner reported GHSA-j456-xh4h-cpf2 (CVSS 8.6) for nltk 3.10.3 before the update\n- updated version: `3.10.4`\n\nValidation:\n- osv-scanner no longer reports GHSA-j456-xh4h-cpf2 after the update\n- `pip install nltk==3.10.4` succeeds and `import nltk` reports 3.10.4\n\nScope: dependency pin update only.\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "Zachary-wW"
            },
            "body": "Hi @katsugtgz, two things before merging this PR:\r\n- Fix the PR title to match our convention.\r\n- Add a quick smoke test for --split-sentences to make sure NLTK 3.10.4 works with our NLTK_DATA setup.",
            "createdAt": "2026-11-04T03:36:14Z",
            "databaseId": 6621850959,
            "updatedAt": "2026-11-04T03:36:14Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/baidu-baige/LoongForge/pull/318#issuecomment-6621850959"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "katsugtgz"
            },
            "body": "Title fixed. On the smoke test: added one, and it reproduces a real failure. The bump is not the cause.\n\nThe `NLTK_DATA` branch of `Encoder.initializer` loads the legacy punkt pickle through a `file:` URL. On nltk 3.10.4 that load fails with `_pickle.UnpicklingError: global 'copy_reg._reconstructor' is forbidden` (`nltk/picklesec.py` rejects the globals used by the legacy pickle). The non-`NLTK_DATA` path still works, because `nltk.load(\"nltk:tokenizers/punkt/english.pickle\")` resolves to the punkt_tab based `PunktTokenizer`.\n\nMeasured on Python 3.12, punkt downloaded fresh into a private `NLTK_DATA` dir:\n\n- nltk 3.10.4, `file:` URL into `NLTK_DATA`: `UnpicklingError`\n- nltk 3.10.3, same load: `UnpicklingError` (so 3.10.3 has the same failure and this PR does not regress it)\n- nltk 3.10.4, `nltk:tokenizers/punkt/english.pickle`: loads as `PunktTokenizer`, sentence split works\n\nAdded `tests/test_preprocess_nltk_data_smoke.py`, which mirrors the tool's punkt download and the `NLTK_DATA` load branch. It is red today for the reason above. It skips when nltk refuses the download because the `NLTK_DATA` path is not private: nltk 3.10 `pathsec` rejects world-writable ancestors, so plain CI tmp dirs cannot exercise this code path.\n\nA fix would be to prepend `$NLTK_DATA` to `nltk.data.path` and load the punkt resource the normal way instead of building a `file:` URL to the pickle, or to move to `punkt_tab`. That is a source change outside this dependency bump, so leaving it with you. Suggest keeping the bump: same behavior on 3.10.3 and 3.10.4 for this path, and it clears GHSA-j456-xh4h-cpf2.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-11-04T08:01:40Z",
            "databaseId": 6625779433,
            "updatedAt": "2026-11-04T08:01:40Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/baidu-baige/LoongForge/pull/318#issuecomment-6625779433"
          }
